ed with  our work who are watching our work  understand you know where we are in the  process  much of the 84-page report dwells on how  the commission is going about its work  and how it will continue gathering  evidence and hearing from witnesses to  those watching the inquiry closely the  theme of the report is not surprising  but the lawyer who represents the  majority of victims families says she  and her clients are disappointed i don't  think any of us expected there to be any  any sort of factual findings or  conclusions drawn in this interim report  but um that it is  essentially silent on any of that is  discouraging  along with in-person hearings the  commission has released thousands of  pages of documents some detailing the  rcmp's confusion as the gunman was  killing 22 people three separate callers  to 9-1-1 tried to tell the maudies the  killer was dressed as one of them and  was driving a replica rcmp vehicle but  he eluded authorities for 13 hours as  officers struggled with technology and  communication before police killed him  after a chance encounter at a gas  station the interim report does include  a reference to mental health and hard  hit communities saying we encourage  governmental and non-governmental  agencies to provide the necessary mental  health trauma and bereavement supports i  expect it will be an area that we will  see recommendations on a final report  once we have more information and had  more opportunity to examine that a  little further upcoming witnesses  include senior rcmp managers who've been  criticized for not initiating an  emergency alert to the public the mass  casualty commission's final report  including lessons learned and  recommendations is due in november  ross lord global news halifax  pandemic recovery canadian style next  how hockey is helping put bars back in  business  jeopardy fans are holding their breath  canadian mateo roach is going for her  20th win in a row tonight her family  already knows what h