ue play-off norm like a normal run  the hospitality industry is still  climbing out of two years of of being  closed being open and close on the  street known in calgary as the red mile  flames and oilers fans are welcome for  now wins for both teams would mean a  battle of alberta in the second round  and a badly needed boom for business  just seeing all the other businesses  including ours being able to  to finally get our legs back underneath  us and rebuild and then this is just a  you know like we couldn't have asked for  a better way to kick start summer of  course a packed house for a week or two  in may won't erase the impacts of two  years of covet restrictions and closures  and there are new challenges for  business owners as well a shortage of  labor rising food costs and expenses  but if a canadian team was able to make  a lengthy run it's huge right you know  the collective memory and collected new  mood is a is a thing right it's just  that much needed energy boost and that  positivity that is as needed right now a  pandemic pallet cleanser like only a  magical playoff push can provide so go  flames go heather yorick's west global  news calgary  that is global national for this monday  i'm donna friesen tonight's your canada  is the morris island conservation area  near arnprior ontario please email your  photos for viewers at globalnational.com  and thanks for watching take care of  yourselves bye-bye  [Applause]  [Music]  you
 

